{"url":"https://files.alkamelcloud.com/wec/results_noticeboard/13_2025/08_8%20Hours%20of%20Bahrain/006_Doc%206%20-%20BRIEFING%20NOTES.pdf","sha256":"4f49e066b9f56e4201a2580a663725cf9550147e4bbedeba78e31aaff5643920","retrieved":"2026-11-24T11:27:11.859Z","pages":[{"page":1,"width":595.2,"height":841.92,"items":[{"s":"1","x":547,"y":792.5,"w":5.9,"h":11},{"s":"2025 – FIA WEC Drivers’ season briefing notes – V2 (04.11.2025)","x":179,"y":803.8,"w":244.6,"h":9.1},{"s":"2025 DRIVERS’ SEASON BRIEFING NOTES – V2","x":115.8,"y":87.8,"w":371,"h":18},{"s":"PIT LANE PROCEDURES","x":49.7,"y":127.4,"w":117.8,"h":11},{"s":"1)","x":67.7,"y":153.6,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"Maximum speed in pit lane: 60 km/h.","x":85.7,"y":153.6,"w":158,"h":10.1},{"s":"2)","x":67.7,"y":165.8,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"Pit lane speed must be respected from pit in loop (60 km/h marker board) to pit out loop (60 km/h marker","x":85.7,"y":165.8,"w":467.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"board).","x":85.7,"y":178.1,"w":31,"h":10.1},{"s":"3)","x":67.7,"y":190.3,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"Red / green at pit exit must be respected at all times.","x":85.7,"y":190.3,"w":223.9,"h":10.1},{"s":"4)","x":67.7,"y":202.6,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"If the red lights are on at pit exit: any car waiting at pit exit must stop before the RFID or 3 meters before the pit","x":85.7,"y":202.6,"w":467.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"exit line.","x":85.7,"y":214.8,"w":35.5,"h":10.1},{"s":"5)","x":67.7,"y":227,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"Cars can be stopped by scrutineering at any time; drivers must respect the signal of the scrutineers.","x":85.7,"y":227,"w":425.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"GENERAL SAFETY AND INCIDENT PROCEDURES","x":49.7,"y":264.5,"w":237.6,"h":11},{"s":"6)","x":67.7,"y":290.6,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"Astroturf / kerbs / track verges take longer to dry than the track.","x":85.7,"y":290.6,"w":268.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"7)","x":67.7,"y":302.9,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"If during a Red Flag, Safety Car, Virtual Safety Car or Full Course Yellow procedures, if you encounter a problem:","x":85.7,"y":302.9,"w":467.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"you must leave the racing line immediately.","x":85.7,"y":315.1,"w":184.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"8)","x":67.7,"y":327.4,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"In case of accident:","x":85.7,"y":327.4,"w":84,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":340.1,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Signal to the marshals that you are OK as soon as possible (‘thumbs up’).","x":121.7,"y":340.1,"w":311.9,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":353,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Do not stay on radio to your team: this can lead to unnecessarily deploying medical services or may","x":121.7,"y":353,"w":431.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"result in a Red Flag.","x":121.7,"y":365.3,"w":83.8,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":378.2,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"If you cannot continue:","x":121.7,"y":378.2,"w":98.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"-","x":148.7,"y":391.2,"w":2.5,"h":11},{"s":"leave the car as soon and as safe as possible.","x":166.7,"y":391.2,"w":194.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"-","x":148.7,"y":404.4,"w":2.5,"h":11},{"s":"Help the recovery operations.","x":166.7,"y":404.4,"w":126.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"-","x":148.7,"y":417.6,"w":2.5,"h":11},{"s":"Car must be left in neutral with steering wheel in position.","x":166.7,"y":417.6,"w":246.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":430.6,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"If you can continue stay in the car so that the marshal can hoist you to a safe place.","x":121.7,"y":430.6,"w":354.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"9)","x":67.7,"y":442.6,"w":8.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"When going through a gravel / run o[ area:","x":85.7,"y":442.6,"w":180,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":455.5,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Zig-Zag your car o[ track before rejoining to drop the gravel / dirt o[ the line.","x":121.7,"y":455.5,"w":322.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"ON TRACK DRIVING STANDARDS","x":49.7,"y":493.2,"w":162.3,"h":11},{"s":"10)","x":67.7,"y":519.4,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Respect across all categories.","x":85.7,"y":519.4,"w":128.5,"h":10.1},{"s":"11)","x":67.7,"y":531.6,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Blue flags (Appendix H ISC Article 2.5.5.e) are to be respected at all times.","x":85.7,"y":531.6,"w":315,"h":10.1},{"s":"12)","x":67.7,"y":543.6,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Discord may be used between competitors to anticipate blue flags.","x":85.7,"y":543.6,"w":286.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"13)","x":67.7,"y":555.8,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"It is up to the faster car to find a way to overtake in tra[ic: slower cars should stick to the racing line.","x":85.7,"y":555.8,"w":424.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"14)","x":67.7,"y":568.1,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Track limits must be respected at all times.","x":85.7,"y":568.1,"w":183.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":581,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Track limits violations will be monitored and listed on a timing page.","x":121.7,"y":581,"w":288.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":593.8,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Track limits are counted by driver by session. The race is considered as one session.","x":121.7,"y":593.8,"w":357.7,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":606.7,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"During FP, warm up or race:","x":121.7,"y":606.7,"w":117.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"-","x":148.7,"y":619.9,"w":2.5,"h":11},{"s":"4","x":166.7,"y":619.9,"w":5.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"th","x":172,"y":616.3,"w":5.2,"h":6},{"s":"o[ence in the session: warning flag.","x":179.3,"y":619.9,"w":153.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"-","x":148.7,"y":633.1,"w":2.5,"h":11},{"s":"5","x":166.7,"y":633.1,"w":5.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"th","x":172,"y":629.5,"w":5.2,"h":6},{"s":"o[ence in the session: report to the Stewards.","x":179.3,"y":633.1,"w":196.7,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":645.8,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"During all sessions, track limit infringements will lead to the deletion of the lap time.","x":121.7,"y":645.8,"w":358.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"TRACK SIDE PANELS","x":49.7,"y":683.5,"w":101.5,"h":11},{"s":"15)","x":67.7,"y":709.7,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Track side panels will be used on most of the tracks visited.","x":85.7,"y":709.7,"w":252.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"16)","x":67.7,"y":721.9,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Track side panels complement marshals’ flags.","x":85.7,"y":721.9,"w":201.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"17)","x":67.7,"y":734.2,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"In case of discrepancy between track side panels, marshal flag or on-board marshalling display, the most","x":85.7,"y":734.2,"w":467.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"restrictive flag will apply.","x":85.7,"y":746.2,"w":105.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"Posted at: 09:37","x":31.9,"y":29.1,"w":92,"h":12},{"s":"Doc No.: 6","x":501.8,"y":29.1,"w":59.3,"h":12}]},{"page":2,"width":595.2,"height":841.92,"items":[{"s":"2","x":547,"y":792.5,"w":5.9,"h":11},{"s":"2025 – FIA WEC Drivers’ season briefing notes – V2 (04.11.2025)","x":179,"y":803.8,"w":244.6,"h":9.1},{"s":"YELLOW AND DOUBLE YELLOW FLAGS – Appendix H of the ISC Article 2.5.5.b","x":49.7,"y":81.1,"w":380,"h":11},{"s":"18)","x":67.7,"y":107.3,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Yellow flag(s) means danger.","x":85.7,"y":107.3,"w":121.7,"h":10.1},{"s":"19)","x":67.7,"y":119.5,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Reduce speed.","x":85.7,"y":119.5,"w":64.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"20)","x":67.7,"y":131.8,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Forbidden to overtake.","x":85.7,"y":131.8,"w":96.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"21)","x":67.7,"y":144,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Double Yellow Flags also mean that marshals and/or vehicles may be exposed, drivers must be ready to stop.","x":85.7,"y":144,"w":465,"h":10.1},{"s":"22)","x":67.7,"y":156.2,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"The onus of proving that any flag is respected is solely on the driver.","x":85.7,"y":156.2,"w":286.5,"h":10.1},{"s":"RED FLAG – FIA WEC Sporting regulations Article 14.3","x":49.7,"y":193.7,"w":263.4,"h":11},{"s":"23)","x":67.7,"y":219.8,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"During free practices, qualifying or warm up, when Red Flag is deployed: all cars to 80 km/h and to come back","x":85.7,"y":219.8,"w":467.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"in pit lane.","x":85.7,"y":232.1,"w":44.5,"h":10.1},{"s":"24)","x":67.7,"y":244.3,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"The Race Director may release the cars from the 80 km/h speed limit once passed the incident to bring all the","x":85.7,"y":244.3,"w":467.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"cars in the pit lane quicker.","x":85.7,"y":256.6,"w":114.8,"h":10.1},{"s":"FULL COURSE YELLOW – FIA WEC Sporting Regulations Article 14.5","x":49.7,"y":294.2,"w":331.6,"h":11},{"s":"25)","x":67.7,"y":320.2,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Once FCY is deployed:","x":85.7,"y":320.2,"w":96.7,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":333.1,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Yellow flags will be waved around the track and FCY board will be presented in the marshal posts.","x":121.7,"y":333.1,"w":414.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":346.1,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Marshal post(s) of the intervention will be under double waved yellow flags.","x":121.7,"y":346.1,"w":320.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":358.8,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"FCY will be displayed on the onboard marshalling system.","x":121.7,"y":358.8,"w":246.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":371.8,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"All cars to slow down to 80 km/h – overtaking is forbidden – there will be a 3 seconds tolerance after","x":121.7,"y":371.8,"w":431.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"the zero countdown for cars to drop at 80 km/h.","x":121.7,"y":384,"w":202.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"26)","x":67.7,"y":396.2,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Pit entry will close when the Race Director announces “FCY will be deployed at…”","x":85.7,"y":396.2,"w":347.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"è","x":120.5,"y":408.5,"w":10.8,"h":10.1},{"s":"In Free Practices, you will be allowed to pit under FCY even if the pit entry closed light is turned on.","x":138.5,"y":408.5,"w":414.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"SAFETY CAR – Appendix H of the ISC Article 2.10 – FIA WEC Sporting Regulations Article 14.6","x":49.7,"y":445.9,"w":454.3,"h":11},{"s":"27)","x":67.7,"y":472.1,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Once Safety car is deployed","x":85.7,"y":472.1,"w":119.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":485,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Yellow flags will be waved around the track and SC boards will be presented in the marshal posts.","x":121.7,"y":485,"w":414.9,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":497.8,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Marshal post(s) preceding the location of the intervention will wave double yellow flags.","x":121.7,"y":497.8,"w":373,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":510.7,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"SC will be displayed on the onboard marshalling system.","x":121.7,"y":510.7,"w":241.9,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":523.7,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Overall leader to slow down around 80 km/h – overtaking is forbidden.","x":121.7,"y":523.7,"w":297.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"28)","x":67.7,"y":535.9,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Weaving to maintain tyre temperature is forbidden in the area(s) a[ected by the incident.","x":85.7,"y":535.9,"w":378.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"29)","x":67.7,"y":547.9,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Weaving to maintain tyre temperature is forbidden during pass around.","x":85.7,"y":547.9,"w":301.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"30)","x":67.7,"y":560.2,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Maximum distance between two consecutive cars is 5-car length gap.","x":85.7,"y":560.2,"w":297.7,"h":10.1},{"s":"31)","x":67.7,"y":572.4,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Pass around will be announced on the timing monitor and by pit wall radio with the two following stages:","x":85.7,"y":572.4,"w":443.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":585.4,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"“Prepare for pass around”: cars eligible for pass around to move to the right-hand side of the track.","x":121.7,"y":585.4,"w":420.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":598.1,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"“Start the pass around”: cars eligible for pass around to start overtaking by the right-hand side the line","x":121.7,"y":598.1,"w":431.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"of cars and the Safety Car.","x":121.7,"y":610.3,"w":112.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":623.3,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Cars doing the pass around must join the back of the queue as quick as possible, in a single line, in a","x":121.7,"y":623.3,"w":431.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"safe way. Bearing in mind that the track is neutralized and that works may still be on going on track or","x":121.7,"y":635.5,"w":431.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"track side.","x":121.7,"y":647.8,"w":44.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":660.5,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Cars that are not doing the pass around will stay on the left-hand side, behind the Safety Car.","x":121.7,"y":660.5,"w":395.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"32)","x":67.7,"y":672.7,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"All cars on track must respect the pit entry closed light, irrelevant of their number of laps completed behind","x":85.7,"y":672.7,"w":467.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"the Safety Car.","x":85.7,"y":685,"w":62.7,"h":10.1},{"s":"33)","x":67.7,"y":697.2,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"At the end of the Safety Car procedure:","x":85.7,"y":697.2,"w":166.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":710.2,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Race Director will instruct “Safety Car in this lap”.","x":121.7,"y":710.2,"w":211.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":722.9,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"The Safety Car will turn o[ the roof lights.","x":121.7,"y":722.9,"w":175.7,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":735.8,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Overtaking remains strictly forbidden until you cross the Line (unless a car is undoubtedly slow).","x":121.7,"y":735.8,"w":409.7,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":748.6,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"It is the obligation of any driver with an obvious problem to stray away from the racing line and not","x":121.7,"y":748.6,"w":431.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"block the cars behind.","x":121.7,"y":760.8,"w":95.3,"h":10.1}]},{"page":3,"width":595.2,"height":841.92,"items":[{"s":"3","x":547,"y":792.5,"w":5.9,"h":11},{"s":"2025 – FIA WEC Drivers’ season briefing notes – V2 (04.11.2025)","x":179,"y":803.8,"w":244.6,"h":9.1},{"s":"VIRTUAL SAFETY CAR – FIA WEC Sporting Regulations Article 14.7","x":49.7,"y":105.6,"w":322.7,"h":11},{"s":"34)","x":67.7,"y":131.8,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Once Virtual Safety Car is deployed","x":85.7,"y":131.8,"w":151.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":144.5,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"A count down will precede the VSC.","x":121.7,"y":144.5,"w":151.9,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":157.4,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Yellow flags will be waved around the track and VSC boards will be presented in the marshal posts.","x":121.7,"y":157.4,"w":420.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":170.4,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Marshal post(s) preceding the location of the intervention will wave double yellow flags.","x":121.7,"y":170.4,"w":373,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":183.1,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"VSC will be displayed in the onboard marshalling system.","x":121.7,"y":183.1,"w":244.5,"h":10.1},{"s":"•","x":103.7,"y":196.1,"w":4.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"All cars to drop to 80 km/h – overtaking is forbidden - there will be a 3 second tolerance after the zero","x":121.7,"y":196.1,"w":431.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"countdown for cars to drop at 80 km/h.","x":121.7,"y":208.3,"w":166.3,"h":10.1},{"s":"STARTING PROCEDURES","x":49.7,"y":246,"w":122.9,"h":11},{"s":"35)","x":67.7,"y":272.2,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Clear instructions will be given during each briefing of the season.","x":85.7,"y":272.2,"w":281.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"36)","x":67.7,"y":284.2,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"The pole position is responsible for the speed of the field.","x":85.7,"y":284.2,"w":244.4,"h":10.1},{"s":"37)","x":67.7,"y":296.4,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Cars must go through the standing start grid boxes markings.","x":85.7,"y":296.4,"w":259.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"38)","x":67.7,"y":308.6,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Race starts once the lights go o[ and when the cars physically cross the Starting Line.","x":85.7,"y":308.6,"w":365.1,"h":10.1},{"s":"PIT ENTRY BEHAVIOUR – FIA WEC Sporting Regulations Articles 12 – 14.3 – 14.5 – 14.6","x":49.7,"y":346.3,"w":417.9,"h":11},{"s":"39)","x":67.7,"y":372.5,"w":13.6,"h":10.1},{"s":"Regarding the “Pit Entry Closed Signal”, in case of failure of the hardware system, once made aware of the","x":85.7,"y":372.5,"w":467.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"problem Race Control will do its best to inform the Competitors as soon as possible via radio and message on","x":85.7,"y":384.7,"w":467.2,"h":10.1},{"s":"the timing monitors.","x":85.7,"y":396.7,"w":86.4,"h":10.1